      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s9yk",
          "text": "What is a Personal Injury?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b9yn",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s9ym",
          "text": "A personal injury is a physical, mental, or emotional injury one party causes another due to negligence or wrongdoing. The purpose of a personal injury claim or a lawsuit is to compensate the injured party monetarily in the hopes of putting them back in the same position they were before their injury.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b9yp",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s9yo",
          "text": "The injured party (plaintiff) in a personal injury lawsuit may be one person, or a group of similarly injured people. The wrongdoer (defendant) may be a person, corporation, or institution. Most personal injury cases settle before going to court.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b9yr",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
